WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.300
Find a seated or resting position that gives the belly room to move.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.005
Loosen anything that feels restrictive if that is comfortable and appropriate.

3
00:00:18.705 --> 00:00:27.775
This is a practice of noticing breathing, not changing how much air you take in.

4
00:00:32.838 --> 00:00:37.033
Let the eyes close or keep a soft gaze.

5
00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:40.813
Feel the support beneath the body.

6
00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:47.778
Notice that breathing is already happening before you direct attention toward it.

7
00:00:56.216 --> 00:01:00.711
Bring one hand to the belly if touch feels helpful.

8
00:01:02.411 --> 00:01:06.691
Otherwise, let both hands rest elsewhere.

9
00:01:08.391 --> 00:01:14.531
There is no correct place to feel the breath and no need for visible movement.

10
00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:27.884
Notice what happens around the belly as an inhale arrives.

11
00:01:29.584 --> 00:01:40.084
There may be a small outward movement, a widening at the sides, a change deeper inside, or very little you can detect.

12
00:01:50.632 --> 00:01:52.072
Notice the exhale.

13
00:01:53.772 --> 00:01:56.612
The belly may soften inward or downward.

14
00:01:58.312 --> 00:01:59.592
It may barely move.

15
00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:05.937
Let each breath finish without pushing out the last air.

16
00:02:16.484 --> 00:02:20.524
Stay with three ordinary breaths.

17
00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:24.184
Receive the inhale as it is.

18
00:02:25.884 --> 00:02:28.444
Follow the exhale as it is.

19
00:02:30.144 --> 00:02:39.619
If breathing feels tight, uneven, shallow, or full, let that be information rather than a problem to solve.

20
00:02:54.386 --> 00:03:00.051
Perhaps the hand can feel movement that attention alone did not notice.

21
00:03:01.751 --> 00:03:04.071
Perhaps touch is distracting.

22
00:03:05.771 --> 00:03:09.796
You can move the hand away at any point.

23
00:03:11.496 --> 00:03:15.096
Choice is part of staying present.

24
00:03:25.644 --> 00:03:31.744
Widen awareness to include the lower ribs and the back of the waist.

25
00:03:33.444 --> 00:03:45.044
Breathing may create a three-dimensional change around the middle of the body, even when one area is clearer than another.

26
00:03:57.701 --> 00:04:00.181
Let the next inhale begin by itself.

27
00:04:01.881 --> 00:04:07.496
Notice its beginning, its continuing, and the moment it turns.

28
00:04:09.196 --> 00:04:13.806
Then notice the exhale beginning without your command.

29
00:04:26.463 --> 00:04:34.958
There may be a brief pause after breathing out, or the next inhale may arrive immediately.

30
00:04:36.658 --> 00:04:38.738
Do not manufacture a pause.

31
00:04:40.438 --> 00:04:42.438
Let the body's timing be enough.

32
00:04:55.095 --> 00:05:05.045
If the mind starts counting, evaluating, or trying to improve the breath, recognize the effort gently.

33
00:05:06.745 --> 00:05:16.590
Return to one simple sensation: movement, pressure, warmth, or contact beneath a hand.

34
00:05:29.247 --> 00:05:35.427
Notice whether the belly feels different at the beginning and end of an exhale.

35
00:05:37.127 --> 00:05:40.977
The difference may be clear, subtle, or absent.

36
00:05:42.677 --> 00:05:45.197
Precision is not required.

37
00:05:57.854 --> 00:06:01.774
For a few breaths, include the whole body.

38
00:06:03.474 --> 00:06:14.924
The belly moves within a body that is supported, hearing sounds, sensing temperature, and occupying a room.

39
00:06:16.624 --> 00:06:19.224
Attention can be steady without becoming narrow.

40
00:06:33.991 --> 00:06:39.571
Return once more to the easiest place to feel breathing around the belly.

41
00:06:41.271 --> 00:06:46.641
Let five breaths pass without adjusting their depth or rhythm.

42
00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:58.826
If discomfort, dizziness, or air hunger appears, stop focusing on breath and orient to the room.

43
00:07:17.812 --> 00:07:20.372
Release any hand from the belly.

44
00:07:22.072 --> 00:07:27.207
Notice the trace of warmth or pressure left by contact.

45
00:07:28.907 --> 00:07:34.402
Feel the body's weight and the ordinary breath continuing on its own.

46
00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.640
Open the gaze more fully.

47
00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.780
You did not need to breathe perfectly.

48
00:07:50.480 --> 00:08:00.000
You practiced meeting the movement that was already here, one unforced breath at a time.
